# Canonicalize .html URLs to clean paths (avoids duplicate-content across
# both /page.html and /page serving the same content with no redirect).
# The "!" forces these to apply even though the .html file physically still
# exists in the repo, Netlify otherwise serves an existing file directly and
# skips the redirect entirely.
/index.html                      /                                 301!
/mortgage-health-check.html      /mortgage-health-check             301!
/home-value-estimator.html       /home-value-estimator              301!
/affordability-check.html        /affordability-check               301!
/closing-costs.html              /closing-costs                     301!
/property-search.html            /property-search                   301!
/homebuyer-guide.html            /homebuyer-guide                   301!
/blog/index.html                 /blog/                             301!

# Individual blog posts moved from /blog/posts/<slug>.html to
# /blog/posts/<slug>/ (directory-index style, so there's structurally only
# one URL per post, no duplicate-content risk). Add one line per old flat
# post URL that was ever live before this change.
/blog/posts/vancouver-mortgage-broker-vs-bank-branch.html   /blog/posts/vancouver-mortgage-broker-vs-bank-branch/   301
